# Deploy plan — runs ON the node itself (not in the VPS compose stack).
# Terminates public TLS for this node's own hostname and forwards to the
# agent, which listens on 127.0.0.1 only (see node.json's listen_addr and
# ../../docs/DEPLOY.md's firewall section — port 8443 is never reachable
# from the public interface directly, only via this local proxy on 443
# or from the WireGuard subnet, for the panel's own control-plane calls).
#
# DNS-01 (not HTTP-01) so port 80 never needs to be open: set
# CLOUDFLARE_API_TOKEN in the environment this runs under (a
# DNS-edit-scoped token, not the account-wide key) — see Caddy's
# cloudflare DNS provider module. Requires the `caddy-dns/cloudflare`
# plugin built in (xcaddy or the official caddy:2-alpine image won't have
# it — build a custom image or use `caddy add-package` first).
#
# Replace node0X.gxhost.com.br with this node's actual public hostname
# before deploying (node01... on the R620, node02... on the Dual Xeon).

node0X.gxhost.com.br {
	tls {
		dns cloudflare {env.CLOUDFLARE_API_TOKEN}
	}
	reverse_proxy 127.0.0.1:8443
}
